# Fixture pattern-rule pack for the scan.sh registry-discovery integration
# test (tests/suites/scan.sh): one quick+compliance-tagged rule, one full-only
# rule, so a `--profile-scan quick` run visibly selects fewer checks than a
# `--profile-scan full` run over the SAME on-disk registry.

id: SAST-GEN-DEMO_QUICK-01
title: Fixture quick+compliance rule
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-95
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: \bdemo_eval\s*\(
dialect: ere
tags: static
tags: quick
tags: compliance
cis: 1.1
remediation: This is a fixture rule; it exists only to prove registry
  discovery and profile filtering compose end to end.
references: CWE-95

id: SAST-GEN-DEMO_FULL-01
title: Fixture full-only rule
severity: low
confidence: medium
cwe: none
owasp: none
pattern: \bdemo_noop\s*\(
dialect: ere
tags: static
remediation: This is a fixture rule with no profile tag, so it runs only under
  `full` - the docs/RULE-FORMAT.md §9.1.3 default.
